        </relations>
    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="10" relname="span">In software design, Intuitiveness means the easy of navigation throughout a program interface without much training or without training at all.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="13" relname="span">This concept in the software development industry is really hard to accomplish</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="14" relname="conjunction">because the end users of software applications are humans,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="14" relname="conjunction">and everybody has a different point of view of intuitiveness.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="15" relname="span">I will say that we can look at Microsoft as one of the pioneers in user interface design with intuitiveness,</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="12" relname="span">for example most of the applications in the Microsoft Office product have a similar Graphical User Interface,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="6" relname="elaboration">the vertical and horizontal menus are similar too.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="12" relname="volitional-result">These features make this software application (Microsoft Office) easy to use and intuitive to the user because of the similarities between applications (Excel, Access, MS Word, etc).</segment>
        <group id="9" type="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="5" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="1" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="14" type="multinuc" parent="2" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="10" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
